<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03DX">Remark <span data-tag="03DX">11.5.0.122</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category, and let us regard the homotopy category $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}$ as enriched over the homotopy category of Kan complexes $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{Kan}}$ (see Construction <a data-tag="01PV" href="/tag/01PV">4.6.8.13</a>). Every functor of $\infty $-categories $\mathscr {F}: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{S}}$ induces an $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{Kan}}$-enriched functor $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\mathscr {F}}: \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \rightarrow \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{S}}} = \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{Kan}}$. Moreover, if $X$ is an object of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, then every vertex $x \in \mathscr {F}(X)$ determines a natural transformation of $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{Kan}}$-enriched functors $\underline{\operatorname{Hom}}_{\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}}( X, \bullet ) \rightarrow \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\mathscr {F}}(\bullet )$, which is an isomorphism if and only if $x$ exhibits $\mathscr {F}$ as corepresented by $X$. Consequently, $\mathscr {F}$ is corepresentable by $X$ if and only if $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\mathscr {F}}$ is isomorphic to $\underline{\operatorname{Hom}}_{\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}}( X, \bullet )$ as an $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{Kan}}$-enriched functor. </p>
</article>
